# expect.stdout: 100\n
# expect.exit: 0
# expect.xfail: feature_coverage.py runs through bootstrap_general.sscript which does not yet recognize `storage module mutable` / `set module`. Direct semsc.py compilation works correctly (`python compiler/semsc.py THIS_FILE --emit-exe /tmp/x.exe && /tmp/x.exe` prints `100\n` and exits 0). Closing means teaching bootstrap_general to emit a module-scope global with load/store across operations.
project ModuleMutableCrossOp
target console
runtime AgentRuntime 0.1
entry console main
error MainError
errorCase MainError ConsoleWriteFailed ConsoleWriteError
storage module immutable zeroInitialValue I64 0
storage module immutable newValueOneHundred I64 100
storage module mutable counterAcrossOperations I64 zeroInitialValue
operation setValueOperation
input operation setValueOperation valueToStore I64
output operation setValueOperation I64
set storage counterAcrossOperations valueToStore
return value valueToStore
operation main
input operation main console Console
output operation main Result ExitCode MainError
effect main write console.stdout
memory main heap no
async main no
purpose operation main "Cross-op: set via helper, then read in main, expect updated value."
invariant operation main "Helper writes 100; main reads back 100."
label startMain
call setHelperCall setValueOperation
argument setHelperCall valueToStore I64 newValueOneHundred
run setHelperCall
ignore value source setHelperCall type I64
call writeUpdatedCall console.writeIntegerLine
argument writeUpdatedCall console Console console
argument writeUpdatedCall value I64 counterAcrossOperations
run writeUpdatedCall
ignore void source writeUpdatedCall
storage module immutable successfulExitCode ExitCode 0
return ok successfulExitCode
